					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "FLOAT\n\nThe Float node generates a floating point number and can also convert booleans, integers and strings to floats.\n\nSo what is a floating point number?\nFloat is short for floating point number, which is just a really fancy way of saying the number has a decimal point in it. It can be either negative or positive. Floats are used very frequently in Wire as many values will range between -1 and 1.\n\n4.31 is a float, -15.12 is a float, the Euler constant is a float.\n5 is not a float, neither is -23 or your birthday.\n\nFloat In is the interactive brother of the Float node, make sure to check that one out too."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 262.664276123046875,
					"width": 803.2596435546875,
					"x": -10.51718521118164062,
